  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the chain for the ticket:\n\n1. **`pkg/registry/core/rest/storage_core.go`** \u2014 the `\"start-service-ip-repair-controllers\"` PostStartHook runs two repair loops (cluster-IP and node-port) via `async.Runner`, and returns `errors.New(\"unable to perform initial IP and Port allocation check\")` if neither loop reports first success within 1 minute (`time.After(time.Minute)`).\n2. **`pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/controller/repairip.go`** \u2014 `RepairIPAddress.syncService` (the `MultiCIDRServiceAllocator` repair loop used when that feature gate is on, which v1.33 carries forward) tries to `Create` an `IPAddress` object for any ClusterIP missing one. This `Create` call goes back through the apiserver's own admission chain.\n3. **`staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/webhook/generic/webhook.go`** and **`.../policy/generic/plugin.go`** \u2014 both admission plugins gate every dispatch on `WaitForReady()`; until their informers (`hookSource`/`source`, namespace informer) have synced, any request \u2014 including the `IPAddresses` create \u2014 is rejected with `admission.NewForbidden(a, fmt.Errorf(\"not yet ready to handle request\"))`. This is the literal source of the observed `ipaddresses.networking.k8s.io \"10.211.95.185\" is forbidden: not yet ready to handle request`.\n4. That failure makes `syncService`/`doRunOnce` return an error, so `RunUntil`'s `onFirstSuccess` callback never fires, `wg.Done` never runs, and the PostStartHook's 1-minute wait expires \u2192 the hook fails.\n5. **`staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/healthz/healthz.go`** \u2014 separately, the `informer-sync` readyz check (`NewInformerSyncHealthz`) fails independently while internal informers haven't finished their initial sync.\n6. **`test/e2e/apimachinery/health_handlers.go`** confirms both `poststarthook/start-service-ip-repair-controllers` and `informer-sync` are required entries in `/readyz`, matching the log line `informer-sync,poststarthook/start-service-ip-repair-controllers check failed: readyz`.\n\n**Root cause of the race**: during the mixed-version rolling upgrade window, a newly-started v1.33 apiserver's own admission-webhook/policy informers haven't synced yet (they need to list/watch against the cluster, which is itself under upgrade load), while its `start-service-ip-repair-controllers` PostStartHook is already trying to write `IPAddress` objects on startup. The write gets rejected by the apiserver's own not-yet-ready admission gate, the repair loop keeps failing, and if it doesn't succeed within the 1-minute PostStartHook deadline, the whole node's readiness flips to `NotReady` \u2014 pulling capacity from the rolling upgrade. Once all nodes are on v1.33 and informer sync races stop competing with fresh restarts, it self-resolves.",
